Preprocessing stage: Datastream sample -> TRTH five-minute measures -> ECB rates -> merged panels.
Run with `python run.py --stage preprocessing` (or `python preprocessing/master.py`) from anywhere;
add `--with-trth` for the tick processing. Every script can also be run on its own from the
repository root.

  python preprocessing/src/d00_gathering/sample.py            -> data/02_preprocessed/sample.csv
      Datastream equities: USD prices and market values, GeoNames coordinates, distances to Ukraine,
      neighbour dummies (nbr_1, nbr_1_or_2), market value >= $10m; returns from priced rows only.
  python preprocessing/src/d01_preprocessing/trth_summary.py  -> data/02_preprocessed/trth/summary/trth_summary.csv
      row/quote/trade counts of the raw .gz files (diagnostic; the numbers are hard-coded in the docs builder).
  python preprocessing/src/d01_preprocessing/trth.py --phase2-workers 8 --output-format parquet --timings
      -> data/02_preprocessed/trth/ukraineNN.parquet. Two phases: (1) stream each .gz into shards per
      RIC x local trading day under data/02_preprocessed/tmp/ (reused if present); (2) per shard:
      cleaning (crossed quotes, negative prices/volumes, stub quotes with spread/mid > 25%, trades
      more than 50% from the prevailing mid; London prints in pounds rescaled to pence), prevailing
      mid within the local day, Lee-Ready direction (quote rule + tick rule) and the Jurkatis (2022)
      full-information direction (vendored in tradeclass/, MIT; build once with
      `python setup.py build_ext --inplace` inside that folder), quoted/effective spread, same-day
      five-minute price impact for both directions, depth, dollar volume, trade-to-trade returns,
      volatility of five-minute midpoint returns, aggregation to five-minute buckets (price_close =
      last trade of the bucket).
        --direction tick|fi|both   trade direction(s) (default both)
        --winsor-ticks             tick-level winsorization at 0.01%/99.99% per RIC (default off)
        --engine polars --temp-format parquet   polars engine (parity-tested against pandas)
        --auto-tune, --chunksize, --phase2-workers, --generate-sample (synthetic test file)
  python preprocessing/src/d01_preprocessing/count_tick_filters.py
      exact counts of the tick filters over the shards (~1.5 h) -> trth/summary/tick_filter_counts.csv
  python preprocessing/src/d01_preprocessing/validate_fi.py
      FI vs Lee-Ready agreement on random real shards -> trth/summary/fi_validation.csv
  python preprocessing/src/d00_gathering/fx_rates.py          -> data/01_raw/handcoded/{fx_rates_ecb,venue_currency}.csv
      daily ECB reference rates in local units per USD (public ECB zip) and the currency, unit factor
      (pence, cents, agorot) and rate source of every venue (country from markets.csv).
  python preprocessing/src/d02_panels/merge.py                -> data/03_output/{intraday,daily}{,_RUS_UKR,_AERO_DEF}.parquet
      per-file merge with the Datastream sample on (RIC, local trading day); local trading hours,
      weekends and exchange holidays; penny screen (Datastream price <= $1 or local price <= 1);
      dollar volume and depth value converted to USD with the ECB rate of the venue's currency
      (implied exchange-day rate for currencies the ECB does not quote); listings quoted in another
      currency than their exchange excluded; realized spread = effective spread - price impact;
      daily aggregation with polars; sample-selection log rows.

Data folders (not in git): data/01_raw (Datastream csv, TRTH .gz, hand-coded markets.csv),
data/02_preprocessed (sample.csv, TRTH shards and outputs), data/03_output (panels). GEO_DATA_ROOT
overrides the data root for trth.py and merge.py (tests on synthetic data).
